    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vzqb18m",
      "content": "Physics is the branch of science that deals with matter, energy, motion, force, heat, light and sound."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1eq7a5f",
      "content": "It explains the natural phenomena occurring around us using scientific laws."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2ovmt0t",
      "content": "Examples: "
    },
    {
      "id": "n3kco54",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Motion of vehicles – Mechanics</li><li>Flow of electricity – Electricity</li><li>Boiling of water – Heat</li><li>Rainbow formation – Optics</li></ul>",
        "Motion of vehicles – Mechanics",
        "Flow of electricity – Electricity",
        "Boiling of water – Heat",
        "Rainbow formation – Optics"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uhn8ch7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PHYSICAL QUANTITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Physical quantities are classified into Fundamental (independent) and Derived (dependent) quantities.",
        "The SI system consists of 7 fundamental units (metre, kilogram, second, ampere, kelvin, mole, candela) and 2 supplementary units (radian, steradian).",
        "Density is calculated as Mass divided by Volume, with the standard SI unit being kg/m³.",
        "Dimensional formulas express physical quantities using fundamental base dimensions [M], [L], and [T].",
        "Dimensional analysis is used to check the correctness of equations and convert units between different systems."
      ],
      "id": "0imlb88"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hos2eeb",
      "content": "A physical quantity is any quantity that can be measured and expressed in numerical value with a unit."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jlhs9yq",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jndaogt",
      "content": "Length = 10 m Mass = 5 kg Time = 20 s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x4h0gdm",
      "content": "Without unit, a number has no physical meaning."
    },
    {
      "id": "f9vxe84",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TYPES OF PHYSICAL QUANTITIES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0t2bzj3",
      "content": "Physical quantities are of two types:"
    },
    {
      "id": "wmecd2m",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Fundamental Quantities",
        "Derived Quantities"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0ru69t5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "FUNDAMENTAL QUANTITIES"
    },
    {
      "id": "zuq9hmp",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "mvxqa5t",
      "src": "/books/Precis/SSC COMPLETE GK/images/image_mvxqa5t.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h917au5",
      "content": "<img></img>Fundamental quantities are basic quantities which cannot be derived from other quantities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bjmndf0",
      "content": "There are seven fundamental quantities in SI system."
    },
    {
      "id": "45uc2jq",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Length – Meter (m)",
        "Mass – Kilogram (kg)",
        "Time – Second (s)",
        "Temperature – Kelvin (K)",
        "Electric Current – Ampere (A)",
        "Luminous Intensity – Candela (cd)",
        "Amount of Substance – Mole (mol)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t6q7s20",
      "content": "Trick to remember:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nkqbi85",
      "content": "\"My Teacher Likes Playing Chess Daily Morning\""
    },
    {
      "id": "idgggc9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "DERIVED QUANTITIES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "htyqg74",
      "content": "Derived quantities are obtained from fundamental quantities. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1wrtikx",
      "content": "Speed = Distance / Time"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Fundamental quantities are independent physical quantities that cannot be defined in terms of other physical quantities.",
      "id": "bpjxq0p"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ikd3k5c",
      "content": "Acceleration = Change in velocity / Time Force = Mass × Acceleration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oyy1np3",
      "content": "Work = Force × Distance Power = Work / Time Density = Mass / Volume"
    },
    {
      "id": "ky40154",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SI SYSTEM OF UNITS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1nmc6ob",
      "content": "SI stands for International System of Units."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i4fxx35",
      "content": "It is accepted globally and used in scientific measurements. It was adopted in the year 1960."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cp4o5vf",
      "content": "Important SI Units: Length – Meter Mass – Kilogram Time – Second Force – Newton Energy – Joule"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3urfs82",
      "content": "Pressure – Pascal"
    },
    {
      "id": "nnxany2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONVERSION OF UNITS"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w61mtdw",
      "content": "1 kilometer = 1000 meters"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xe3zhh9",
      "content": "1 meter = 100 centimeters"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5vf7v8g",
      "content": "1 kilogram = 1000 grams"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ycrb1k4",
      "content": "1 hour = 3600 seconds"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Fundamental Quantities",
        "Derived Quantities"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Definition",
          "Independent quantities that do not rely on other physical quantities.",
